WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.295
Hi, I'm Radar!

00:00:02.295 --> 00:00:06.317
Needle 3 is a tiny tool-calling model that scores its own calls.

00:00:06.317 --> 00:00:09.669
Here's how, and why a local fine-tune loses that score.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:14.620
A small post-hoc head reads the whole network, prompt and finished call

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.385
together, and judges the call after it is made.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.279
The head reads the prompt and the finished call at all twenty-one

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:25.888
depths: the embedding, plus each of the twenty blocks.

00:00:26.308 --> 00:00:30.182
Eighty-four probe vectors, one per depth and lane, each pool the whole

00:00:30.182 --> 00:00:31.474
trace into one summary.

00:00:31.894 --> 00:00:35.891
Four query vectors attend across those summaries, and their results project down

00:00:35.891 --> 00:00:37.223
to a single logit.

00:00:37.643 --> 00:00:41.751
Confidence is the minimum of that score and the decoder's own probability.

00:00:41.751 --> 00:00:44.490
A call is accepted only when both agree.

00:00:46.192 --> 00:00:48.493
The head reads the backbone under stop gradient.

00:00:48.493 --> 00:00:51.656
Training it cannot move one weight of the model it judges.

00:00:52.076 --> 00:00:56.000
It was trained in a separate run and merged in at step ten thousand.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.402
No gradient path reaches it.

00:00:57.822 --> 00:01:02.014
A local LoRA moves accuracy eighteen to thirty-six points, so the old

00:01:02.014 --> 00:01:04.808
head would predict failures that no longer happen.

00:01:05.228 --> 00:01:08.510
So the build deletes the head, and confidence comes back as None.

00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:14.874
The local path also exports at four bits, because its packer refuses anything else.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:18.926
A tuned archive is sixty-three point four four megabytes, against thirty-five

00:01:18.926 --> 00:01:20.399
point three four shipped.

00:01:21.892 --> 00:01:24.440
Calibration is a fit, and a fit needs samples.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.121
The head has to be retrained with the model, on your own tools.

00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:34.540
To recap: a detached probe judges each call, a local fine-tune drops

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.506
it, and exports at four bits.

00:01:36.926 --> 00:01:39.027
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:39.027 --> 00:01:39.627
I'm Radar.

00:01:39.627 --> 00:01:39.927
Bye!
